        "question": "Describe two economic benefits of physical activity.",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "1. Reduced cost to the health service. Regular physical activity lowers rates of coronary heart disease, type 2 diabetes, stroke, several cancers, obesity and mental health difficulties. Every case prevented is a cost avoided in GP visits, medication, hospital treatment and long-term care, and physical inactivity costs health systems very large sums each year. Money spent on facilities and participation programmes therefore reduces future public spending.\n2. Economic activity and employment. Sport and physical activity support a substantial industry — retailers, gyms, clubs, coaches, physiotherapists, facility staff, event organisers and the hospitality businesses that trade around events — and this generates employment and tax revenue. Activity also raises productivity in the wider economy, because active employees take fewer sick days and are less likely to leave work early through ill health.",
