        "label": "(b) (i)",
        "question": "In a named physical activity of your choice, identify two common injuries and explain how they could be treated.",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "Named physical activity: soccer.\nInjury 1: ankle sprain — the ligaments on the outside of the ankle are overstretched when the foot rolls inwards. Treatment: apply PRICE. Protect the player by removing them from the field, rest the ankle and take weight off it, apply ice wrapped in a damp cloth for fifteen to twenty minutes, compress with an elastic bandage, and elevate the leg above the level of the heart. Refer for medical assessment if the player cannot bear weight.\nInjury 2: a cut or laceration to the knee or shin. Treatment: put on gloves, apply direct pressure with a sterile dressing to stop the bleeding, clean the wound with saline once bleeding is controlled, cover it with a sterile dressing, and follow blood-borne pathogen protocol by removing the player from the field and replacing any blood-stained kit before they return. Refer for medical attention if the wound is deep, gaping or will not stop bleeding.",
