        "label": "(c)",
        "question": "In a named physical activity of your choice, describe two benefits of flexibility training.",
        "marks": 10,
        "model": "Named physical activity: hurling.\n1. Increased range of movement at the joints, which improves technique and performance. Greater flexibility through the shoulders, trunk and hips allows a fuller backswing and follow-through when striking, so the player generates more power and greater distance on a puck-out or a long-range point. It also allows a player to reach and control a ball that would otherwise be out of range.\n2. Reduced injury risk and better recovery. Muscles and tendons that can move through a full range are less likely to be strained when a joint is forced beyond its normal position — in a tackle, a stretch for a ball or a sudden change of direction. Hamstring and groin strains are among the most common injuries in hurling, and adequate flexibility around the hip is one of the main protective factors. Regular flexibility work also helps maintain muscle length after heavy training, so the player returns to the next session in better condition.",
