        "question": "Outline three rules and regulations of a named physical activity of your choice.",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "Named physical activity: basketball.\n1. A team may have a maximum of five players on court at any one time, with unlimited substitutions made only during a stoppage in play.\n2. A team in possession has 24 seconds in which to attempt a shot that hits the rim; failing to do so is a shot-clock violation and possession is turned over.\n3. A player may not travel — that is, take more than two steps while holding the ball without dribbling — and may not dribble, stop, and then begin dribbling again (a double dribble). Both are violations and result in a turnover.",
