        "label": "(c) (ii)",
        "question": "Name one dietary supplement and outline two advantages of using that supplement.\nAdvantage 1.\nAdvantage 2.",
        "marks": 10,
        "model": "Supplement: creatine monohydrate.\nAdvantage 1: it increases the store of phosphocreatine held in the muscle, which is the fuel the ATP-PC system uses during maximal effort. A larger store extends the duration of maximal power output slightly and, more importantly, speeds recovery of that store between efforts, so the athlete can complete more high-quality repetitions in a session and maintain sprint speed better across a match.\nAdvantage 2: because it allows a greater total training load at high intensity over weeks and months, it produces greater gains in muscular strength, power and lean muscle mass than the same training without it. It is one of the most researched supplements, is not prohibited, and is relatively inexpensive — but it must be batch-tested and certified, since contamination during manufacture is a recognised route to an inadvertent anti-doping violation under strict liability.",
