        "question": "Explain two different methods of physical fitness training that could be used to help prepare athletes for performance in a physical activity of your choice.",
        "marks": 8,
        "model": "Physical activity: hurling.\n1. Interval training. The player performs repeated short maximal efforts — for example 10 × 40 metre sprints with 45 seconds of walking recovery — alternating high-intensity work with incomplete recovery. This matches the intermittent demand of the game, developing both the anaerobic systems that supply the sprints and the aerobic capacity that clears by-products between them, so the player can repeat efforts in the last quarter.\n2. Weight (resistance) training. The player lifts against progressively heavier external resistance — squats, deadlifts, presses — at 80% or more of one-repetition maximum for low repetitions. This develops the muscular strength and power underlying striking distance, jumping for a dropping ball and holding position in contact, and it strengthens tendon and connective tissue, reducing injury risk.",
