        "label": "(a)",
        "question": "During the NFL (American National Football League) Combine event athletes are put through a series of physical and mental tests which give them the opportunity to showcase their athleticism and mental preparedness to coaches and team managers.\nName and justify the selection of four tests that you would include in a physical fitness test battery for a physical activity of your choice.\nTest Justification for test",
        "marks": 12,
        "model": "Physical activity: soccer.\n1. Yo-Yo Intermittent Recovery Test. Justified because soccer is an intermittent sport requiring repeated high-intensity runs with brief recovery; this test measures precisely that capacity, rather than steady-state endurance, and it correlates well with the high-intensity distance players actually cover in matches.\n2. 30-metre sprint test with 10-metre split. Justified because most decisive actions — getting to a through ball, closing down, breaking clear — are short sprints, and the 10-metre split separates acceleration from maximum velocity, which are trained differently and matter to different positions.\n3. Illinois agility test. Justified because soccer demands repeated rapid changes of direction under control, and this test measures whole-body agility over a distance and duration similar to a match action, unlike a straight-line sprint.\n4. Countermovement vertical jump. Justified because it measures lower-body explosive power, which underlies jumping for headers, accelerating and changing direction, and because it is quick, repeatable and widely used to monitor neuromuscular fatigue across a season.",
