        "model": "Fitness test: the multi-stage fitness test (bleep test).\nDescription: Two lines are marked 20 metres apart on a flat, non-slip surface. The performer runs continuously between the two lines, turning on the line and timing each 20-metre shuttle to arrive as the recorded bleep sounds. The bleeps start slowly and get progressively faster at the end of each level, so the required running speed increases every minute. The performer must place a foot on or over the line on each bleep; if they fail to reach the line on two successive bleeps, or can no longer continue, the test is stopped. The score is the level and shuttle reached, which is converted to a predicted VO2 max using standard tables and compared against normative data for age and sex. It measures cardiovascular endurance because it forces the heart, lungs and circulatory system to keep supplying oxygen at a steadily rising workload until the athlete can no longer sustain it.",
