        "model": "1. Carry out a risk assessment of the venue and equipment beforehand, and act on it. The organisers walk the route or inspect the pitch and facilities in advance, checking the playing surface for hazards, the security of posts and goals, and the condition of equipment, and they check the weather forecast so an event can be postponed in dangerous conditions. Anything identified is fixed, fenced off or the event modified before participants arrive.\n2. Put appropriate medical and emergency provision in place. Qualified first aiders or medical staff must be present in numbers matched to the size of the event, with a stocked first aid kit and a defibrillator available and staff trained to use it. There must be a written emergency action plan naming who takes charge, how emergency services are called, where the access route for an ambulance is, and how participants are accounted for — and it must be communicated to all staff and volunteers before the event begins.",
