        "marks": 4,
        "model": "Hegemonic masculinity is the dominant, socially accepted idea of what it means to be a man in a given society — the version of masculinity treated as the norm against which all men are measured. In Western society it is built around physical strength, toughness, competitiveness, aggression, emotional restraint, heterosexuality and being the provider. In sport it shapes which activities are seen as properly masculine — contact and strength-based sports such as rugby, boxing and hurling — and discourages boys from dance, gymnastics or aerobics. It also encourages men to play through injury and to hide pain or anxiety, because admitting to either conflicts with the expected image.",
