        "model": "Hegemonic femininity is the dominant, socially accepted idea of what it means to be a woman — the version of femininity treated as the norm for women in a given society. It is built around slimness, grace, an appearance-focused attractiveness, gentleness and passivity rather than physical assertion. In sport it makes activities that build visible muscle or involve contact appear unfeminine, so girls are steered towards dance, gymnastics, camogie and athletics and away from rugby, boxing and weightlifting. Women who compete in strength or contact sports often have their femininity questioned, and the pressure to conform to an appearance ideal is one of the main reasons girls drop out of sport in adolescence.",
