        "question": "Describe an activity that could be used to improve performance in a named skill from a physical activity of your choice. You may use a diagram.",
        "marks": 8,
        "model": "Physical activity: basketball. Skill: the lay-up. Activity: a progressive lay-up drill. Players form a line at the wing, roughly 45 degrees from the basket. Each player receives a pass, takes the ball in two hands, and performs the right-hand lay-up using the correct footwork — outside foot, inside foot, drive the inside knee up and lay the ball high off the top corner of the square on the backboard. The first phase is done from a standing start with no dribble, so attention is on the footwork and the release. The second phase adds one dribble into the same footwork, the third adds a defender giving passive pressure, and the fourth runs the drill at game speed from a fast break. Coaching points: two-hand catch, outside foot first, drive the knee up on take-off, and lay the ball softly off the top corner of the square with a high release.",
