        "label": "(b)",
        "question": "Name a sports supplement used by athletes and justify why athletes might use this supplement.",
        "marks": 4,
        "model": "Supplement: creatine monohydrate. Athletes use creatine because it increases the store of phosphocreatine held in the muscle, and phosphocreatine is the substrate the ATP-PC system uses to resynthesise ATP during maximal effort. A larger store slightly extends the duration of maximal power output and, more importantly, speeds the restoration of that store between efforts, so the athlete completes more high-quality repetitions in a session and maintains sprint speed better across a match. Over weeks of training the greater accumulated load at high intensity produces measurably larger gains in strength, power and lean muscle mass. It is one of the most researched supplements, is effective for repeated high-intensity activity, is not prohibited and is inexpensive — but it must be batch-tested and certified, since contamination during manufacture is a recognised route to an inadvertent anti-doping violation under strict liability.",
