        "marks": 5,
        "model": "1. Time-wasting when in the lead — taking an excessive time over a restart, substitution or free kick to run down the clock.\n2. Sledging or verbally distracting an opponent to break their concentration before a free, a serve or a penalty. (Deliberately slowing a restart, gamesmanship over an opponent's injury, or claiming a decision the player knows is wrong are equally acceptable.)",
