        "label": "(a) (iii)",
        "question": "Outline three safety regulations in a named physical activity of your choice.",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "Named physical activity: hurling.\n1. Approved protective equipment is compulsory: all players at every age grade must wear a helmet with a faceguard that meets the required standard, and it must be worn correctly with the chin strap fastened.\n2. The pitch and equipment must be checked and made safe before play: goalposts must be padded and securely anchored, the playing surface must be inspected and cleared of hazards, and any damaged hurleys must be removed from use.\n3. Qualified first aid provision must be present: a trained first aider with a stocked kit and access to a defibrillator, along with a concussion protocol under which any player suspected of concussion is removed immediately and not permitted to return that day.",
        "diagram": "",
