        "marks": 6,
        "model": "Performance-related component of fitness: power. Fitness test: the standing (countermovement) vertical jump test.\nDescription: a measuring board or jump mat is used. The athlete first stands side-on to the wall with the feet flat and reaches up as high as possible with the nearer arm, and this standing reach height is recorded. Chalk or a marker is applied to the fingertips. The athlete then stands with feet shoulder-width apart, dips rapidly into a half squat with an arm swing, and jumps vertically as high as possible, marking the wall at the highest point. No run-up or step is permitted. Three attempts are given with a full recovery between each, and the best is recorded. The score is the difference between the standing reach height and the highest jump mark, measured in centimetres, and it is compared against normative tables for age and sex. It measures power because it requires the leg muscles to generate the greatest possible force in the shortest possible time in a single explosive effort.",
