        "question": "Physical Education is a concept of physical activity.\nExplain Physical Education in this context.",
        "marks": 4,
        "model": "As a concept of physical activity, Physical Education is the planned, timetabled curriculum subject in which young people learn about, through and in movement. What distinguishes it from the other concepts is its educational purpose and its compulsory, structured nature. It is taught by a qualified teacher, follows a syllabus built around stated learning outcomes, is assessed, and reaches every student regardless of ability, interest or family resources — unlike sport, which is competitive, voluntary and governed by an external body, or leisure and recreation, which are undertaken freely in a person's own time. Its aim is not to produce a winner but to develop movement competence across a range of activities together with the knowledge, understanding, skills and dispositions needed for lifelong participation. Because it is the one setting that reaches everyone, it is the foundation on which participation in the other concepts is built.",
