        "model": "1. It prepares the body physically — raising heart rate, body temperature and blood flow to the working muscles, which increases the speed and force of muscle contraction and the range of movement available at the joints.\n2. It reduces the risk of injury and prepares the athlete mentally — warm muscles and mobilised joints are far less likely to be strained by a sudden maximal effort, and the warm-up gives the athlete time to focus attention on the task and rehearse the skills they will need.",
