        "question": "Define ability.",
        "marks": 4,
        "model": "Ability is an inherited, relatively enduring trait or capacity that underpins a person's potential to acquire and perform skills — for example coordination, reaction time, balance, flexibility or speed of limb movement. Abilities are largely genetically determined, change relatively little with practice, and are general rather than specific to one activity. They provide the raw material on which learned skills are built, but they are not skills themselves: two people with the same abilities will perform very differently depending on how much they have practised.",
