        "question": "List four statements that comply with the Principles of Ethical Practice, and could be included in a code of ethics for sport.",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "1. All participants, coaches, officials and spectators will treat each other with respect, regardless of ability, sex, ethnicity, religion, disability or background.\n2. Decisions of officials will be accepted without dissent, and any concern will be raised afterwards through the proper channels rather than during play.\n3. The club is committed to fair play and to competing within both the rules and the spirit of the activity; doping, cheating and gamesmanship will not be tolerated.\n4. The welfare of participants, particularly children, takes precedence over results; all coaches will be vetted and trained in safeguarding, and every participant will be given a genuine opportunity to take part.",
