        "marks": 4,
        "model": "Confidence is a performer's belief in their own ability to execute the skills required and to achieve the outcome they are aiming for in a given situation. It is built primarily from previous successful experience, and also from watching others succeed, from encouragement and feedback, and from the performer's physiological and emotional state at the time. It is specific rather than general — a performer can be highly confident in one skill or situation and not in another.",
