        "label": "(c) (i)",
        "question": "Parkrun is a 5km run arranged in many locations around the world. The Parkrun happens on Saturday morning and everyone is welcome to participate. Parkrun is an example of a mass participation sports event.\nOutline two benefits of mass‐participation sports events, like Parkrun.",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "A mass participation sports event is an organised event in which a very large number of people take part at the same time, open to a wide range of ages and abilities, with the emphasis on taking part and completing rather than on winning. Parkrun fits this because it is free, weekly, open to anyone who registers, held at a fixed time in many locations, and welcomes walkers, first-timers and club runners in the same event, with no qualification standard and no requirement to compete.",
