        "question": "Explain intrinsic feedback.",
        "marks": 2,
        "model": "Intrinsic feedback is the information a performer receives from within their own body during and immediately after a movement — from the muscles, joints, balance and vision. It is the 'feel' of the skill: a hurler knows from the contact through the hurley whether the strike was clean before they look up to see where the ball went.",
