        "question": "Outline why two of these principles of training are important when planning training sessions in a physical activity of your choice.\nYou must refer to two of those explained in (iii).",
        "marks": 4,
        "model": "Physical activity: Gaelic football. Individuality matters because a senior squad contains players of very different training ages; loading a 19-year-old with the same strength and conditioning volume as a 27-year-old risks injury and burnout in the player the team most needs to develop, so sessions are planned in individualised groups. Progressive overload matters because a squad that repeats the same running and gym loads all season stops improving; the coach must increase load in planned steps across the pre-season so players arrive at the championship measurably fitter, while allowing enough recovery for the adaptation to occur.",
