        "label": "(a)",
        "question": "The FITT formula is used to plan training programmes.\nDefine each part of the FITT formula.\nF I T T",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "F — Frequency: how often the training is done, usually the number of sessions per week.\nI — Intensity: how hard the training is, measured for example as a percentage of maximum heart rate or of one-repetition maximum.\nT — Time: how long each session or effort lasts, i.e. the duration of the training.\nT — Type: the kind of training used, chosen to match the component of fitness being developed, for example continuous running, interval training or weight training.",
