        "question": "Define the concept of physical activity, leisure and recreation.",
        "marks": 4,
        "model": "Physical activity is any bodily movement produced by skeletal muscle that requires energy expenditure above resting level — including sport, exercise, active travel, work and household tasks.\nLeisure and recreation is physical activity undertaken voluntarily in a person's free time, chosen for enjoyment, relaxation and personal satisfaction rather than for competition or external reward. It is usually informal, without rules, officials or a recorded result — a walk, a swim, a cycle or a kickabout.",
