        "model": "First aid treatment for an ankle sprain: apply the PRICE protocol. Protect — stop the player immediately and remove them from the field so the joint is not loaded further. Rest — take all weight off the ankle and do not allow the player to run it off. Ice — apply a cold pack wrapped in a damp cloth for fifteen to twenty minutes, repeated every two to three hours for the first forty-eight hours, to reduce pain and limit swelling by narrowing the blood vessels. Compression — apply a firm elastic bandage from the toes upwards to control swelling, checking that toes stay warm and pink so circulation is not restricted. Elevation — raise the leg above the level of the heart to help drain fluid away from the joint. Refer the player for medical assessment if they cannot bear weight, if there is severe pain over the bone, or if there is significant deformity, since a fracture must be ruled out. Avoid heat, alcohol, running and massage in the first forty-eight hours.",
