        "marks": 6,
        "model": "Reason: the periodisation of her season meant she was peaking for the NCAA championship final rather than for the World Championship. The case study describes her intention to gear a season towards a target competition, which is exactly what periodisation involves — training is built in phases so that volume falls and intensity rises into a taper before one identified event, and the athlete arrives both fit and fresh. Where the World Championship fell outside that peak, she would have been competing while still carrying training load or after the peak had passed. Supporting reasons available from the case study include the extra year of training and physical development between the races, and the difference in the competitive context — the NCAA final came at the end of a college season built towards it, with rounds and rivals that produced a fast race.",
        "diagram": "",
